        1,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lehigh%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Wilson of Webster City built the Crooked Creek Railroad’s 3‑foot gauge line in 1880, later widened it and joined Iowa’s longest interurban line in 1916.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12,
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lehigh%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lehigh was surrounded by coal mines until the early 20th century and housed a large clay sewer pipe factory that operated until the 1980s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lehigh%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Historic Sanborn maps from 1915 and 1931 let you see Lehigh’s downtown layout and businesses as they were over a century ago.",
